    "salt": "dUxtXiHrulxK97B4sQyTBg==",
    "text": "Glas Ghaibhleann is a cow from Irish mythology. Her milk was so plentiful that it fed multitudes and made abundant butter. She could cross three of Ireland's four provinces in one day. Place names across the land, often beginning with Glas, recall her path. She offered milk to every person in need, filling any vessel, large or small. Some see her as an image of the Irish land itself.",
